                    vectors from each lesion image using a                      
                    pretrained ResNet18 (with its final                         
                    classifier removed) and train a simple                      
                    logistic regression to predict                              
                    malignant vs. non‐malignant. We                             
                    evaluate performance via 5-fold                             
                    stratified cross‐validation using                           
                    AUROC. After reporting the mean and                         
                    standard deviation of the ROC AUC, we                       
                    retrain on the full data and expose a                       
                    `predict(image_dir)` function that                          
                    returns malignant probabilities for any                     
                    new folder of images. Finally, we                           
                    demonstrate saving these probabilities                      
                    to `submission.csv`.                                        
                    Results: The code executed successfully                     
                    without any errors. The model achieved                      
                    a good cross-validated ROC AUC of                           
                    approximately 0.834, indicating                             
